+When a reviewer reports no findings for a patch agent, the controller appends
+`work-leaf: is this feature done? yes/no` to the patch-agent session and selects that session. A
+`yes` or `y` response records the feature as done, appends `work-leaf: feature marked done`, and keeps
+the response inside the controller instead of sending it to the agent backend. A `no` or `n` response
+appends `work-leaf: feature remains open. Type the next request to reopen work.` without closing the
+session. Any other response to the prompt, or the next message after a closed feature, appends
+`work-leaf: feature reopened` and continues through the normal selected-agent send path. Completion
+prompt and state-marker transcript lines are append events even when the same text already appears in
+the session, so repeated review completions remain visible to frontends that consume incremental
+events.
